          Springdale hires the truck, they check whether the shop is real.
          They look for the same business name, the same hours, and a real
          license, on the site and on the Google Business Profile. If those
          facts disagree, the shop looks unfinished.
        </p>
        <p>
          Consistent facts are the proof. A slogan is not. Publishing the
          license you already hold is a facts task. It is not legal advice,
          and it is not a reading of how a profile gets ordered.
        </p>
        <p>
